# Dell U4025QW — both HID interfaces of the upstream hub MCU pair.
#
# Match by the hidraw VID:DEV pair (kernel HID enumeration), not by USB
# VID:PID, so all I/O goes through the kernel hid-generic driver — the
# same path Dell's hidapi-based binary uses.
#
# The U4025QW exposes two HID interfaces on different USB sub-paths of
# its internal hub. They are *not* the same chip:
#   - DEV_1100: RTS5409S upstream hub MCU. Owns the cal_auth handshake,
#     opens an i2c tunnel to the FL5500 scaler, stages downstream-MCU
#     ISP shims (HUB1 → 0xD4, HUB2 → 0xD6) over the i2c tunnel, stages
#     the HUB ISP shim (64 KB) into its own RAM via 0xC8, and is the
#     interface the engine talks to for the install. **This is the
#     primary; updatable.**
#   - DEV_1101: RTS5418E secondary hub MCU. Same protocol family but a
#     different chip; owns the HUB4 ISP shim (128 KB) staging via 0xC8,
#     fires its own bootloader-entry trigger on its own hidraw fd, and
#     runs in lock-step with the primary during the post-bootloader
#     bulk flash phase. The plugin pairs the two as parent/child during
#     `device_registered` so the primary's `write_firmware` can reach
#     in and stage HUB4 onto the secondary. **Updatable-hidden so
#     fwupd's device list stays clean.**
[HIDRAW\VEN_0BDA&DEV_1100]
Plugin = dell_monitor_rt
Name = U4025QW
VersionFormat = plain

[HIDRAW\VEN_0BDA&DEV_1101]
Plugin = dell_monitor_rt
Name = U4025QW (secondary)
VersionFormat = plain
Flags = updatable-hidden
